Here’s a full, **beginner-to-advanced guide** to creating tables in HTML, including **styling, merging cells, accessibility, responsiveness, and interactivity**.

---

## ✅ 1. Basic HTML Table

```html
<table border="1">
  <tr>
    <th>Name</th>
    <th>Age</th>
    <th>City</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Shlok</td>
    <td>21</td>
    <td>Pune</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Anya</td>
    <td>22</td>
    <td>Mumbai</td>
  </tr>
</table>
```

---

## ✅ 2. Semantic Table (No `border`)

```html
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Product</th>
      <th>Price</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Pen</td>
      <td>10</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Notebook</td>
      <td>40</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
```

---

## ✅ 3. Add CSS Styling

```html
<style>
  table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
  }

  th, td {
    border: 1px solid #999;
    padding: 10px;
    text-align: left;
  }

  thead {
    background-color: #f4f4f4;
  }

  tr:nth-child(even) {
    background-color: #f9f9f9;
  }
</style>
```

---

## ✅ 4. Merging Cells (colspan & rowspan)

```html
<table border="1">
  <tr>
    <th rowspan="2">Name</th>
    <th colspan="2">Marks</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <th>Math</th>
    <th>Science</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Shlok</td>
    <td>85</td>
    <td>90</td>
  </tr>
</table>
```

---

## ✅ 5. Responsive Table (Overflow Scroll on Small Devices)

```html
<style>
  .table-container {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  table {
    min-width: 600px;
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
  }

  th, td {
    border: 1px solid #ccc;
    padding: 8px;
  }
</style>

<div class="table-container">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Course</th>
        <th>Duration</th>
        <th>Instructor</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>HTML</td>
        <td>1 Week</td>
        <td>Dr. Smith</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
```

